'''Icestorm''' is a [[cold]] [[spell]] only available through {{il|The Whispering Ice}}. 

==Skill functions and interactions==
'''Intelligence''': Icestorm's defining characteristic is that, while it is only ever a level 1 skill, its overall effectiveness can be increased with points into the [[Intelligence]] stat. In addition to the percentage-increase to all spell damage for every 10 points of Intelligence from The Whispering Ice staff itself, the skill also gains a flat 5 to 7 added cold damage for every 10 points of Intelligence. For every 100 points of Intelligence, the skill gains a base 0.1 second to its duration.

'''Support Gems''': As with {{il|Jaws of Agony}}, [[support gem]]s do not have to be linked together in order to apply to the innate skill Icestorm. This means that an unlinked six-[[socket]] The Whispering Ice is just as effective for modifying the effect of Icestorm as a six-linked The Whispering Ice. 

'''Empower/Enhance/Enlighten''': Due to Icestorm being an innate property on The Whispering Ice, and not an actual socketed gem, {{il|Empower Support}}, {{il|Enhance Support}}, and {{il|Enlighten Support}} do not affect Icestorm.

'''Totem, Mine, Trap''': Icestorm can be supported by {{il|Spell Totem Support}}, {{il|Trap Support}}, {{il|Blastchain Mine Support}}, {{il|High-Impact Mine Support}}. 

'''[[Area of Effect]]''': Increased AoE will increase both the area in which the ice shards randomly fall and also the radius of the individual ice shard damage. Full [[spell damage]] is done at any point within the AoE of a shard, however due to the fact that enemies take up an area, and not simply a point, less spell damage is dealt to any given enemy as area increases. This is why, contrary to popular belief, increasing the AoE of Icestorm decreases the average number of [[hit]]s to single target. However, this is only true if the enemy remains within the AoE of Icestorm for its whole duration. Increasing the AoE can therefore be advisable for movement-heavy fights.

'''[[Skill Duration|Duration]]''': Increasing duration with either [[support]]s or [[passive]]s will increase the total number of ice shards that fall before the spell ends. The duration of icestorms is also increased by 0.1 second per every 100 points of Intelligence. Additionally, the length of time the [[chilled ground]] remains also increases or decreases. 

'''[[Damage Effectiveness]]''': Flat damage from secondary sources like 'added damage' supports or [[herald]]s apply at 100% of their values. This includes the added cold damage for every 10 points of Intelligence.

'''Damage per Second''': Due to the complexity of estimating actual DPS of the skill including all possible factors, in-game tooltip shows only average damage per hit of one ice shard, with actual DPS of the skill being considerably higher.

===Strategy===
{{il|Cast while Channelling Support}} allows skipping the long cast time, in the extreme case: going from 0.75 second cast times down to .30 second cast times.
